      "message": "fix(app): every operation's approach starts over the setup's WCS origin\n\nMost mill generators seed their path at X0 Y0 on the clearance plane:\nthe world origin. The opening rapid started there, so the viewport, the\nsimulation link, the CL START line and the post's StartX/Y/Z all read\nthe world origin instead of G54. Posted blocks were already correct (a\npost writes move ends only).\n\nToolpath::seat_approach moves the start of an opening rapid that\nleaves that seed to the WCS origin (wcs_context, the origin the post\nsubtracts), read in the local frame for a 3+2 path. It runs after\ngeneration and before the yaw exit, the fixture routing and verify.\nPaths that open elsewhere (holes, plasma, sinker, lathe, wire, rotary,\n3D roughing) and a zero-length seed rapid are untouched.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/wcs_start.rs (2D face and 3D parallel fail\non main) and two seat_approach tests in crates/cl/tests/origin_approach.rs.\n\nFixes #2382\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
